@startuml NC-Status
' =============================================================================
' Nonconformity management — how the app calculates an NC's status
' Complements NC-Flowchart.puml: here, the exact rule and its order of priority.
' English version of ../Statut-NC.puml: same structure, keep both in step.
'
' Rendering: PlantUML 1.2023 or later (checked with 1.2023.13 and 1.2026.8).
'
' Same colour code as the flowchart:
'   <<user>>  user action in the app
'   <<auto>>  status set or recalculated by the app, with no data entry
' Orange shapes are decisions; here, all of them are automatic tests by the app.
'
' Status values are translated; the README glossary gives the app's own
' (French) values. Sources and full legend: README.md, in this folder.
' =============================================================================

' Second line of a box: the screen or formula behind the action.
!function $tech($text)
!return "<size:10><color:#555555>" + $text + "</color></size>"
!endfunction

!pragma useVerticalIf on
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ConditionEndStyle hline
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor<<user>> #DCEBFA
  BorderColor<<user>> #2E6DA4
  BackgroundColor<<auto>> #EEEEEE
  BorderColor<<auto>> #8A8A8A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFE7C2
  DiamondBorderColor #B26B00
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B560
}

title NC status — how the app calculates it

start
:Save an analysis or an action\n$tech("ecrEditionAnalyse, ecrEditionAction"); <<user>>
note right
  An NC's status is never entered by hand:
  it is read-only in ecrEditionNC,
  and a new NC starts as “Open”.
end note

if (NC “Awaiting signature” or “Closed”?) then (yes)
  :Status unchanged:\nit belongs to the report workflow; <<auto>>
  note right
    The report workflow sets “Awaiting signature”
    and “Closed”, and returns the NC to
    “Effectiveness check” on refusal or revision
    (flowchart, phases 5 and 6).
  end note
  stop
else (no)
endif

:Find the target status: the first true condition wins\n$tech("App.Formulas › StatutNCCible"); <<auto>>
note right
  Corrective action = type “Corrective action”
  only. An immediate action is containment
  and is not counted.
end note

if (At least one corrective action, all “Approved”\nor “Rejected”, at least one “Approved”?) then (yes)
  :“Effectiveness check”; <<auto>>
elseif (At least one corrective action\nwith a start date?) then (yes)
  :“CAPA in progress”; <<auto>>
  note right
    The calculation can go backwards: a new
    corrective action on an NC in “Effectiveness
    check” brings it back here. This is how a
    rejected follow-up reopens the CAPA.
  end note
elseif (At least one corrective action?) then (yes)
  :“CAPA defined”; <<auto>>
  note right
    Known defect: a “Rejected” action counts.
    An NC whose only corrective action was
    rejected therefore stays “CAPA defined”, or
    “CAPA in progress” if the action had started.
  end note
elseif (At least one analysis?) then (yes)
  :“Under analysis”; <<auto>>
else (no)
  :“Open”; <<auto>>
endif

if (Target status different from the current one?) then (yes)
  :Write the new status:\nthe label changes on screen, without a reload; <<auto>>
else (no)
  :Write nothing:\nno modified date, no extra history version; <<auto>>
endif
stop

legend bottom left
  |= Colour |= Who acts |
  |<#DCEBFA>          | User action in the app |
  |<#EEEEEE>          | Status set or recalculated by the app, with no data entry |
  |<#FFE7C2>          | Automatic test by the app |
  The “Approved” and “Rejected” judgments remain human:
  the app sets a status from facts, never from judgments.
endlegend
@enduml
